# The build context is the repository root, so this is the file Docker reads.
# A .dockerignore inside web/ is not consulted for a root context.
#
# The context was 428 MB without this: the host's node_modules for two
# projects, the staged binaries, the git history and the live database.

# The image installs its own dependencies from the lockfiles. The host's
# copy must not come along — it would overwrite the image's own install
# with one built for a different platform.
**/node_modules

# Build output and caches.
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.vite

# Runtime state: the SQLite database and the uploaded assets. They are not
# source, and they must never reach the build context.
data/
backups/

# Locally staged binaries — mkcert and caddy, fetched by the setup script.
tools/bin/

# The git history is not needed to build the image.
.git

# TLS material, in case it is ever left in the tree.
deploy/caddy/certs/*.pem

# The documentation and the design records are not part of the image.
docs/
*.md
